From 923ec0e7af5f921c69234e6d481e841d5a2362cc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Lothian <mike@fireburn.co.uk>
Date: Wed, 3 Jun 2026 22:04:46 +0100
Subject: [PATCH v4 1/2] rust: crypto: add AES-128, AES-CTR, AES-CMAC, SHA-256, and
 HMAC bindings

Add synchronous bindings for the library crypto a driver needs to
authenticate a device before it is allowed to drive it: AES-128 single
block encryption, AES-128-CTR, AES-CMAC, SHA-256 and HMAC-SHA256.

aes_ctr() and aes_encrypt() take a transparent union that bindgen cannot
express, and the AES-CMAC one-shot prepares a key struct that Rust cannot
construct, so those three go through helpers. SHA-256 and HMAC-SHA256 are
plain extern functions and are bound directly.

The CTR binding is the one a protocol uses directly rather than through a
mode built on top of it, which crypto/aes-ctr.h names as a supported
caller. It takes the initial counter block and advances it past the data,
so a caller can carry one keystream across several calls.

Secret wipes its bytes when dropped, and zeroize() forwards to
memzero_explicit(), for which Rust has no equivalent.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5
Signed-off-by: Mike Lothian <mike@fireburn.co.uk>
---
 lib/crypto/Kconfig              |  20 ++++
 rust/bindings/bindings_helper.h |   3 +
 rust/helpers/crypto.c           |  59 +++++++++++
 rust/helpers/helpers.c          |   1 +
 rust/kernel/crypto.rs           | 172 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 rust/kernel/lib.rs              |   1 +
 6 files changed, 256 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 rust/helpers/crypto.c
 create mode 100644 rust/kernel/crypto.rs

